install.body:
Once it's installed, the current Windows account can use the background service, without asking for permission again, to:
· end processes of any user (except critical system processes) and set their priority and efficiency mode;
· start and stop any Windows service and change its startup type, including services of security software and Windows Update;
· close any IPv4 TCP connection, and see the file locks and network traffic of every process.

Other programs running as a standard user under this account can use these operations too, which effectively gives the account some administrator rights. Install it only on an account that you use yourself. The service starts with Windows. Installing requires administrator permission; the service can be uninstalled in Settings later.
